	],
	"notice": "Use USB MIDI or a DIN MIDI interface. Match the MIDI channel and enable the required MIDI transmit/receive settings. Use the part-channel MIDI implementation. Cutoff/resonance are CC3/CC9. Shared envelope sliders are mapped to the AMP bank. Wave encoder relative messages are left unmapped. The included K-25m dock uses virtual note defaults.  GUI controls generate MIDI into the chain; route that chain to a MIDI output to control the hardware. DIN devices normally appear under the MIDI interface name, so select the profile manually. Unmapped physical buttons and switches have stable SVG IDs for future bindings. Positions are schematic. Note surfaces use virtual defaults; use MIDI learn to match the hardware octave or configuration.",
